NASA and historical material
----------------------------

This is an independent, unofficial historical archive. It is not a NASA
product, and NASA does not endorse it. NASA names and mission identifiers are
used descriptively. The NASA Insignia, Logotype, and Seal are not used as this
project's brand identifiers.

Many source photographs, recordings, documents, data products, models, and
textures in or referenced by this repository are U.S. government works or
NASA-released public-domain material. That statement does not apply
automatically to contractor-authored diagrams, third-party editorial text,
curation, or other separately protected contributions. The authoritative
per-record rights statement, source URL, local path, hash, and processing note
is src/missions/apollo11/source-manifest.json. The Phase 7 rights audit records
any unresolved distribution boundary.

Model and texture truth boundaries
----------------------------------

- Saturn V: NASA-released generic visualization model with reconstructed
  semantic splits. It is not certified AS-506 flight CAD.
- Lunar Module: NASA-released generic Apollo LM visualization model with a
  reconstructed stage split. It is not certified LM-5 Eagle geometry.
- Command/Service Module: reconstructed from NASA-published references and a
  NASA-released print kit. It is not NASA CAD and is not certified Columbia
  CSM-107 geometry.
- Earth and Moon textures: modern NASA imagery-based composites. They are not
  instantaneous reconstructions of the appearance at a 1969 mission time.

Reproducible processing recipes, hashes, LODs, and decoder versions are indexed
in docs/audit/MODEL-PROCESSING-NOTES.md and the asset manifest.

